  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "What will be the acceleration due to gravity at a depth $d$, where $g$ is acceleration due to gravity on the surface of earth?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1F0rZ",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{g}{\\left[1+\\frac{d}{R}\\right]^2}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8FNve",
      "text": "\r\n$g\\left[1-\\frac{2 d}{R}\\right]$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OkFQt",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{g}{\\left[1-\\frac{d}{R}\\right]^2}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xiENS",
      "text": "\r\n$g\\left[1-\\frac{d}{R}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acceleration due to gravity at the surface of earth,\r\n$$\r\ng=\\frac{G M}{R^2}=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\rho G R\r\n$$\r\n$$\r\n\\left[\\because M=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi R^3 \\cdot \\rho\\right]\r\n$$\r\nWhere, $\\rho=$ density of earth.\r\nAcceleration due to gravity at depth $d$ from the surface of earth,\r\n$$\r\ng^{\\prime}=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\rho G(R-d)\r\n$$\r\nFrom Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\ng^{\\prime}=g\\left[1-\\frac{d}{R}\\right]\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
